        </div>

        <!-- OVERVIEW -->
        <section class="section" id="hephaestus-overview">
          <div class="section-title">Overview</div>
          <div class="overview-card">
            <p>Hephaestus is a <strong>Legendary Support</strong> of the <strong>Hearts faction</strong> whose entire kit revolves around a unique zone-control system: he deploys <span class="highlight">3 mechanical devices</span> at battle start and activates them one by one with each Ultimate cast, building toward a field-wide <strong>Fusion effect</strong> that simultaneously buffs his team and debuffs all enemies.</p>
            <p>He is not a healer, not a DPS, and not a standard buffer. He is a <em>Zone-Control Support</em> who shapes the battlefield by creating persistent areas that regenerate HP and Energy for allies while reducing ATK Power and ATK Speed for enemies standing inside them. His Weak Point Analysis automatically targets and binds the highest-damage enemy while shredding their resistances. His Force Field Shield scales its damage reduction with how many devices are active.</p>
            <p>The critical design feature is his <strong>Forge Anchor</strong>: Hephaestus cannot move freely. If he leaves his Forge, he is teleported back into an intercepted state. In exchange, he gains unlimited attack range and reduced damage taken while in Focus state. His immobility is not a weakness to be worked around -- it is the foundation his entire defensive identity is built upon.</p>
            <p>Hephaestus rewards investment and patience. He needs 3 Ultimate casts to reach Fusion and Relic Lv3 to cycle those Ultimates at a competitive speed. In the right composition with the right investment, the Fusion effect is described as potentially one of the strongest team-wide buff states in the game.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- LORE -->
        <section class="section" id="hephaestus-lore">
          <div class="section-title">Lore &amp; Background</div>
          <div class="mechanic-box">
            <div class="mechanic-label">God of Fire and Forge -- Greek Mythology</div>
            <p style="font-size:14px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-bottom:14px; line-height:1.5;">Hephaestus is the Greek god of fire, the forge, craftsmanship, and invention -- the only Olympian god depicted as physically imperfect and the only one who works for a living. Thrown from Olympus as an infant (accounts differ on whether by Zeus or Hera), he built his forge inside a volcano and created the most magnificent weapons and artifacts in mythology. His workshop was staffed by golden automatons of his own making -- the earliest conception of mechanical servants. The game draws directly on this mythology for his mechanical device system.</p>
            <ul class="mechanic-list">
              <li><em>Ultimate Domain</em> (终极领域) channels his dominion over crafted machinery -- the 3 devices are his automatons deployed onto the battlefield, each extending his reach and power</li>
              <li><em>Undying Forge</em> (不灭锻炉) is the literal anchor of his mythology -- Hephaestus belongs at his forge, and the game enforces this by returning him there if he strays</li>
              <li><em>Source Resonance</em> (源流共鸣) reflects the inexhaustible fire of his volcanic workshop -- his Energy never truly runs dry</li>
              <li><em>Weak Point Analysis</em> (弱点解析) embodies the master craftsman's eye: identifying structural flaws and exploiting them with surgical precision, stripping the enemy's defenses</li>
              <li><em>Force Field Shield</em> (力场护盾) is the protective craft side of his duality -- the same hands that forge weapons also build shields for those he fights alongside</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- DEVICE FUSION SYSTEM -->
        <section class="section" id="hephaestus-fusion">
          <div class="section-title">Core Mechanic -- The Device and Fusion System</div>
          <div class="mechanic-box">
            <div class="mechanic-label">How the Device Loop Works</div>
            <ul class="mechanic-list">
              <li>At battle start, <strong>3 inactive mechanical devices</strong> are placed on the field via Ultimate Domain's passive component.</li>
              <li>Each cast of Ultimate Domain activates the <strong>farthest inactive device</strong>, expanding its area of effect. Allies inside regenerate HP and Energy per second; enemies inside suffer ATK Power and ATK Speed reduction.</li>
              <li>Active device count directly scales two other skills: <strong>Weak Point Analysis</strong> extends its Bind duration by a set amount per active device, and <strong>Force Field Shield</strong> increases its damage reduction bonus per active device.</li>
              <li>When all 3 devices are active, they <strong>merge into a single field-wide Fusion effect</strong>: immediately reduces all enemies' damage rate by a percentage and boosts friendly damage rate and ATK Speed for a duration.</li>
              <li>Subsequent Ultimate casts after Fusion <strong>also trigger the Fusion effect</strong> -- meaning the first Fusion is the floor, not the ceiling.</li>
              <li>The loop: <strong>Source Resonance accelerates Energy -- Ultimate Domain activates devices -- devices scale Weak Point and Shield -- 3rd activation triggers Fusion -- Undying Forge Lv3 reduces Ult Energy cost -- next Fusion comes faster.</strong></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="mechanic-box" style="margin-top:16px; border-color: rgba(180,130,80,0.25); background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(180,130,80,0.06), rgba(180,130,80,0.04));">
            <div class="mechanic-label" style="color: var(--gold-light);">The Forge Anchor -- Immobility as Identity</div>
            <ul class="mechanic-list">
              <li>If Hephaestus moves away from the Forge, he is <strong>teleported back</strong> and enters an intercepted state (briefly unable to act). This is not punishable displacement -- it is a guaranteed return.</li>
              <li>While at the Forge he enters <strong>Focus state</strong>: unlimited attack range across the entire field and reduced damage taken. These bonuses only apply while he remains at the Forge.</li>
              <li>This makes Hephaestus effectively <strong>immune to displacement skills</strong> such as knockbacks and pulls -- he will always return to his Forge regardless of what the enemy does to him.</li>
              <li>The tradeoff is total: he cannot reposition, he cannot retreat, and he cannot chase. His Forge placement at battle start is the only moment where positioning matters. Place him in the backline center.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- SKILLS -->
        <section class="section" id="hephaestus-skills">
          <div class="section-title">Skill Breakdown</div>
          <div class="skills-grid">

            <div class="skill-card ultimate">
              <div class="skill-header">
                <img class="skill-icon" src="/skills/hephaestus_skill_1.png" alt="Ultimate Domain" />
                <span class="skill-name">Ultimate Domain</span>
