              <div class="skill-note">
                Relic Lv3 is the defining investment breakpoint. The Energy cost reduction on Ultimate Domain directly accelerates the pace of device activation and therefore the timing of the Fusion trigger. Without it, Hephaestus reaches Fusion much later and the fight tempo feels slow. Lv2 is a meaningful quality-of-life improvement; Lv4 deepens his survivability further.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="skill-card">
              <div class="skill-header">
                <img class="skill-icon" src="/skills/hephaestus_skill_2.png" alt="Weak Point Analysis" />
                <span class="skill-name">Weak Point Analysis</span>
                <span class="skill-badge badge-skill">Active</span>
              </div>
              <p class="skill-desc">
                Fires a laser at the enemy currently dealing the most damage, <span class="highlight">binding</span> them for a duration. Each active device on the field extends the Bind duration by a set amount. Also reduces the target's <span class="highlight">Physical and Magical resistance</span>.
              </p>
              <div class="skill-upgrade-block">
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv2</span><span class="upgrade-text">Physical and Magical resistance reduction increased.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv3</span><span class="upgrade-text">Bind duration extension per active field device increased.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv4</span><span class="upgrade-text">Physical and Magical resistance reduction increased again.</span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-note">
                The auto-targeting logic is key: Weak Point Analysis always locks onto the highest-damage enemy, making it highly effective in auto-battle content. With all 3 devices active, the Bind duration can become extremely long -- potentially locking the enemy carry for an entire fight phase. The resistance shred applies to both damage types, benefiting any DPS in the composition regardless of their damage source.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="skill-card">
              <div class="skill-header">
                <img class="skill-icon" src="/skills/hephaestus_skill_3.png" alt="Force Field Shield" />
                <span class="skill-name">Force Field Shield</span>
                <span class="skill-badge badge-skill">Active</span>
              </div>
              <p class="skill-desc">
                Heals the most wounded allied unit and reduces the <span class="highlight">damage they receive</span> for a duration. For each active device on the field, the damage reduction effect is additionally increased by a percentage.
              </p>
              <div class="skill-upgrade-block">
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv2</span><span class="upgrade-text">Healing effect increased.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv3</span><span class="upgrade-text">Damage reduction from active field devices increased.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv4</span><span class="upgrade-text">Healing effect increased again.</span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-note">
                Like Weak Point Analysis, Force Field Shield scales directly with active device count. With 3 devices active the damage reduction bonus becomes substantial, effectively creating a damage-mitigation shield on the most endangered ally at the moment it matters most. The auto-targeting on the most wounded unit makes it reliable in auto-battle without requiring manual coordination.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="skill-card">
              <div class="skill-header">
                <img class="skill-icon" src="/skills/hephaestus_skill_4.png" alt="Source Resonance" />
                <span class="skill-name">Source Resonance</span>
                <span class="skill-badge badge-skill">Passive</span>
              </div>
              <p class="skill-desc">
                Hephaestus's <span class="highlight">Energy recovery speed</span> is increased by a percentage.
              </p>
              <div class="skill-upgrade-block">
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv2</span><span class="upgrade-text">Energy recovery rate increase is higher.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv3</span><span class="upgrade-text">Energy recovery rate increase is higher again.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv4</span><span class="upgrade-text">Gains initial Energy at the start of battle.</span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-note">
                The passive foundation of the device loop. Faster Energy means earlier first Ult cast, which means earlier first device activation, which means earlier Bind scaling on Weak Point Analysis and Shield scaling on Force Field. Lv4 initial Energy is a significant quality-of-life spike -- Hephaestus reaches the first activation faster and the Fusion window shifts earlier in the fight.
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>

          <div class="mechanic-box" style="margin-top: 20px;">
            <div class="mechanic-label">Skill Upgrade Priority</div>
            <ul class="mechanic-list">
              <li><strong>1. Undying Forge (Relic)</strong> -- Lv3 Energy cost reduction is the most impactful single upgrade in the kit; reach this before farming stars or skill levels</li>
              <li><strong>2. Source Resonance (Passive)</strong> -- Lv4 initial Energy accelerates the first device activation and compresses the Fusion timeline</li>
              <li><strong>3. Ultimate Domain (Ultimate)</strong> -- Lv4 amplifies the Fusion payoff directly; every subsequent Fusion cast is stronger</li>
              <li><strong>4. Weak Point Analysis (Active)</strong> -- Lv3 extends Bind duration per device; with 3 active devices this can lock the carry for a prolonged window</li>
              <li><strong>5. Force Field Shield (Active)</strong> -- Lv3 increases damage reduction scaling per device; lower priority than the loop accelerators above</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- RATINGS -->
        <section class="section" id="hephaestus-ratings">
          <div class="section-title">Mode Ratings</div>
          <div class="rating-grid">
            <div class="rating-card">
              <div class="rating-mode">PVE / Campaign</div>
              <div class="rating-cell"><span class="rating-badge rating-s">S</span></div>
              <div class="rating-desc">Strong sustain zones and device scaling shine in longer PvE fights; slower ramp means 2nd/3rd team use in early campaign</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rating-card">
              <div class="rating-mode">Boss Fights</div>
              <div class="rating-cell"><span class="rating-badge rating-s">S</span></div>
              <div class="rating-desc">Long fights guarantee Fusion -- resistance shred on boss is extremely valuable for the entire team's DPS output</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rating-card">
              <div class="rating-mode">PVP</div>
              <div class="rating-cell"><span class="rating-badge rating-a">A</span></div>
              <div class="rating-desc">Immobility limits adaptability; strong against static comps but hard-countered by dive-burst teams that end fights before Fusion</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size:12px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-top:12px; font-style:italic; text-align:center;">* Ratings based on CN server skill analysis. Released CN Version 1.8. Niche S-tier with correct investment and composition.</p>
        </section>

        <!-- POSITIONING -->
        <section class="section" id="hephaestus-positioning">
          <div class="section-title">Recommended Positioning</div>
          <div class="pos-grid">
            <div class="pos-card">
              <div class="pos-mode">Backline Center -- Fixed Position</div>
              <p>Hephaestus has no choice in positioning beyond his starting slot: his Forge is placed in front of him at battle start, and he cannot leave it. Place him in the <strong>backline center</strong> position to ensure the Forge spawns in a location that maximizes device coverage across the widest area of the field.</p>
              <p>Incorrect starting position is the only positioning mistake available to make. Once the Forge is placed, his position is fixed for the entire fight. The Forge's teleport-back mechanic means the opponent cannot displace him -- all investment in placement pays off reliably.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="pos-card">
              <div class="pos-mode">Formation Structure</div>
              <p><strong>Front:</strong> A stationary or taunt-based tank (Prometheus, Geb) -- these units benefit from the device zones and keep enemies inside the debuff areas. Prometheus in particular creates a Bunker Core as a second immobile anchor alongside Hephaestus.</p>
              <p><strong>Mid:</strong> DPS units (Isis, Hecate, Hladgunnr) positioned to benefit from device heal zones while their damage is amplified by Weak Point Analysis's resistance shred on the primary target.</p>
              <p><strong>Back:</strong> Hephaestus plus a secondary support. The goal is to ensure the Forge zone covers as much of the formation's natural combat area as possible at battle start.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- COMPS -->
        <section class="section" id="hephaestus-comps">
          <div class="section-title">Suggested Comps</div>
          <div class="comp-list">
            {HEPHAESTUS_COMPS.map(comp => (
              <div class="comp-entry">
                <div class="comp-entry-header">
                  <span class="comp-label">{comp.label}</span>
                  <p class="comp-reason">{comp.reason}</p>
                </div>
                <div class="comp-hero-row">
                  {comp.heroes.map(id => (
                    <a href={`/heroes/${id}`} class="hero-chip">
                      <img src={heroImage(id)} alt={heroName(id)} loading="lazy" />
                      <span class="hero-chip-name">{heroName(id)}</span>
                    </a>
                  ))}
                </div>
                {comp.notes?.length > 0 && (
                  <ul class="comp-notes">
                    {comp.notes.map(n => <li>{n}</li>)}
                  </ul>
                )}
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- STRENGTHS / WEAKNESSES -->
        <section class="section" id="hephaestus-strengths">
          <div class="section-title">Strengths &amp; Weaknesses</div>
          <div class="sw-grid">
            <div class="sw-card strengths">
              <div class="sw-title">Strengths</div>
              <ul class="sw-list">
                <li>Unique zone-control mechanic -- no other hero in Motto Immortal deploys persistent, deployable buff/debuff zones of this kind</li>
                <li>Fusion effect provides a field-wide simultaneous team damage boost and enemy damage reduction -- potentially the strongest single team-buff state in the game at full activation</li>
                <li>Weak Point Analysis auto-targets the highest-damage enemy and shreds both physical and magical resistance -- highly effective in auto-battle without manual input</li>
                <li>Effectively immune to displacement skills -- Forge teleport-back means knockbacks and pulls cannot permanently remove him from his position</li>
                <li>Device zones scale two other skills directly: longer Bind on Weak Point Analysis and higher damage reduction on Force Field Shield</li>
                <li>Boss content specialist -- long fights guarantee Fusion and resistance shred on the boss amplifies the entire team's DPS output simultaneously</li>
                <li>Source Resonance Lv4 initial Energy and Undying Forge Lv3 Energy reduction stack to significantly compress the Fusion timeline with correct investment</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="sw-card weaknesses">
              <div class="sw-title">Weaknesses</div>
              <ul class="sw-list">
                <li>Slow ramp-up: 3 Ultimate casts required to reach Fusion -- burst-heavy PvP compositions can end the fight before the third activation</li>
                <li>Total immobility: Forge placement at battle start is the only positioning decision; poor starting placement means poor device zone coverage for the entire fight</li>
                <li>Zero personal damage output -- entirely dependent on teammates for DPS; a weak carry pool collapses his value to sustain and CC only</li>
                <li>Strongly relic-dependent: without Relic Lv3 the Ult rotation feels slow and the Fusion trigger is delayed significantly</li>
                <li>Anti-heal effects partially neutralize his device HP regeneration, reducing his sustain value in compositions or against teams running heal-denial skills</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- SYNERGY -->
        <section class="section" id="hephaestus-synergy">
          <div class="section-title">Synergy Considerations</div>
          <div class="synergy-list">
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Prometheus</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">The strongest frontline anchor for Hephaestus. Both heroes are positionally static -- Prometheus as a self-rooted tank and Hephaestus as Forge-bound -- creating a Bunker Core that forces the enemy to engage into both simultaneously. Prometheus absorbs the damage, Hephaestus heals him through device zones and Force Field Shield, and both benefit from the Hearts faction bonus.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Geb</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">Taunt-tank who draws enemies into the device zones where their ATK Power and ATK Speed are reduced. Geb holds enemies in place within the debuff area while taking reduced damage thanks to Force Field Shield. A reliable frontline anchor that keeps the device zones populated with debuffed targets.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Poseidon</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">Gather effect compresses enemies into the device zones, maximizing simultaneous debuff exposure. Multiple enemies inside the same zone receive ATK Speed reduction at once, compounding Hephaestus's team-wide debuff efficiency. One of the strongest tools for maximizing device zone coverage in a single cast.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Dionysus</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">Energy support that stacks directly with Source Resonance to create an ultra-fast Ult rotation. More Energy means earlier device activations, earlier Fusion, and earlier repeat Fusion casts. The primary Energy-loop partner for Hephaestus in speed-focused compositions.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Pan</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">AoE crowd control that chains with Weak Point Analysis. Pan's CC keeps enemies inside device zones for sustained debuff exposure, and his silence delays enemy Ultimates while Hephaestus ramps toward Fusion. Core PvE control partner.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Isis</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">Stationary or low-mobility DPS that benefits maximally from device zone heal sustain. Isis can operate from a fixed position within the zone's range while her damage is amplified by the resistance shred from Weak Point Analysis and the Fusion damage rate boost once all 3 devices are active.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Hecate</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">DoT damage source whose 10-second Ultimate benefits from the extended fight duration Hephaestus's sustain zones create. Multiple Hecate Ultimate casts in a single long fight compound with the Fusion ATK Speed boost to create an escalating damage loop. Ideal for boss content and prolonged PvE stages.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Mengpo</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">Revival extends fight duration -- longer fights mean more Fusion triggers, more Weak Point Analysis casts, and more device heal ticks. Mengpo's Samsara acts as insurance that the team survives long enough to reach the third device activation when the fight would otherwise end before Fusion.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <div class="divider-ornament">&#10022; &#10022; &#10022;</div>

        <!-- PLAYSTYLE SUMMARY -->
        <section class="section" id="hephaestus-playstyle">
          <div class="section-title">Playstyle Summary</div>
          <div class="overview-card">
            <p>Hephaestus is a <em>set-and-forget zone architect</em> whose output accumulates passively over a fight rather than spiking on demand. The optimal approach is simple: place him in the backline center, let the Forge spawn, and focus entirely on the Ultimate rotation -- activate the farthest device with each cast, prioritizing maximum zone coverage. The three secondary skills (Source Resonance, Weak Point Analysis, Force Field Shield) all operate automatically on correct targets without input.</p>
            <p>The critical expression of skill is compositional, not mechanical. Building a team that can survive until the third activation is the primary design challenge. Slow ramp-up is the defining weakness: compositions that reach Fusion are extremely strong; compositions that are eliminated before the third cast never experience his peak. In PvE and boss content this is rarely an issue -- long fights are his natural habitat. In PvP the timing question becomes the core strategic risk.</p>
            <p>The common mistakes are structural, not reactive: placing him forward, building Attack stats instead of HP and Energy Recovery, running him in fast burst compositions where Fusion is unreachable, and ignoring Relic Lv3. Correct investment path is clear -- reach Relic Lv3 before investing in stars or raw stat upgrades. The Energy cost reduction on Ultimate Domain has more fight-deciding impact than any stat point, because it moves the Fusion trigger forward in time and all of Hephaestus's value compounds from that moment.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

      </div>
    </div>
    )}

